<title>A bistable population model</title>
<variantControl numVariants="1" />

<p>We can describe the evolution of a bistable population with a dynamical system of the form
<md>
  <mrow>\frac{dx}{dt} &amp;= rx(x-\alpha)(\beta-x)</mrow>
  <mrow>x(0) &amp;= x_0</mrow> 
</md>
where <m>r</m> is the growth rate and <m>\alpha</m> and <m>\beta</m> are the non-zero equilibria.  The number <m>x_0</m> is the initial population size.</p>


<p>Substituting in numbers for the parameters, we can write the dynamical system as
  <odeSystem name="ode" initialconditions="$x0" tolerance="0.01" displaydigits="6">
    <rightHandSide>$r*x*(x-$alpha)($beta-x)</rightHandSide>
  </odeSystem>
  You can change the values of the parameters by opening up the Advanced Options, below.
</p>

<p>In both panels of the simulation, the <ref to="doenet:82MrUSX6Y2kQrMerT3xvqn">state space</ref> of the dynamical system is represented by a <text extend="$stateLine.styleDescription" /> line.  A <text extend="$x0onLine.styleDescriptionWithNoun" /> represents the initial condition <m>x(0) = $x0</m> and a <text extend="$aOfTOnLine.styleDescriptionWithNoun" /> represents the population size <m>x(t)</m> at time t, which you can change via the slider or by dragging the  <text extend="$aOfTOnLine.styleDescriptionWithNoun" /> in the right panel.</p>

<p>The left panel shows the state line of the model by itself, while the right panel is a plot of the <ref to="doenet:82S5kKvMFZgTae6rHgvyF4">state variable</ref> versus time.</p>


<setup>
  <clampNumber name="x0" lowerValue="0" upperValue="$xmax">100</clampNumber>
  <function extend="$ode.numericalSolution" name="f" />
  <number name="rDefault">0.000001</number>
  <number name="alphaDefault">2000</number>
  <number name="betaDefault">500</number>
  <number name="tmaxDefault">10</number>
  <number name="xmaxDefault">3200</number>
  <math name="stateVarAtT">$$f($t)</math>
</setup>

<sideBySide margins="3%">

<stack>
<graph displayYAxis="false" aspectRatio="4" xmin="-0.05$xmax" xmax="$xmax" showNavigation="false">
  <xLabel>x</xLabel>
  <lineSegment endpoints="(0,0) ($xmax, 0)" fixed="true" name="stateLine" />
  <point x="$x0" y="$zeroFixed" name="x0onLine" labelPosition="lowerright" applyStyleToLabel="true">
    
      <constrainToGrid />
    
    <label><m>x_0 = $x0</m></label>
  </point>
  <point styleNumber="3" x="$stateVarAtT" y="$zeroFixed" draggable="false" layer="1" name="aOfTOnLine" labelPosition="upperright" applyStyleToLabel="true">
    <label><m>x($t) = <math displayDecimals="1" extend="$stateVarAtT" /></m></label>
  </point>
</graph>

<p><m>x_0 =</m> <mathInput bindValueTo="$x0" /></p>

<slider name="t" width="200px" from="0" to="$tmax" step="0.1" labelIsName="true" />

<p><math displaydecimals="1" functionSymbols="x">x($t) = $ft_NaN_to_infinity[1][1]</math></p>
    
    
<p>
<updateValue name="on" hide="$timeAnimation.animationOn" type="boolean" target="$timeAnimation.animationOn" newValue="true">
  <label>Animate</label>
</updateValue>
<updateValue name="off" hide="not $timeAnimation.animationOn" type="boolean" target="$timeAnimation.animationOn" newValue="false">
  <label>Stop</label>
</updateValue>
</p>

</stack>

<graph xmax="$tmax" xmin="-0.1$tmax" ymax="$xmax" ymin="-0.1$xmax" showNavigation="false">
  <xLabel>t</xLabel>
  <yLabel>x</yLabel>
  
  <lineSegment endpoints="(0,0) (0, $xmax)" fixed="true" />

  <function extend="$f" stylenumber="2" />
  <point x="$zeroFixed" y="$x0" applyStyleToLabel="true">
    
      <constrainToGrid />
    
    <label><m>x_0 = $x0</m></label>
  </point>
  <point styleNumber="3" x="$t" y="$stateVarAtT" layer="1" applyStyleToLabel="true">
    <label><m>x($t) = <math displayDecimals="1" extend="$stateVarAtT" /></m></label>
  </point>
</graph>

</sideBySide>

<aside>
<title>Advanced options</title>

<sideBySide margins="0%" widths="50% 20% 20%">
<!--   <stack>
    <p>The dynamical system describing the dynamics of the bistable population is
    </p>
    <odesystem name="ode" initialconditions="$x0" tolerance="0.01" displaydigits="6" >
      <righthandside>$r*x*(x&#x2D;$alpha)(x&#x2D;$beta)</righthandside>
    </odesystem>

    <p>In terms of parameters, the equation is
    <me>\frac{dx}{dt} = rx(x&#x2D;\alpha)(x&#x2D;\beta).</me>
    You can change growth rate <m>r</m> and the equilibria <m>\alpha</m> and <m>\beta</m>, 
    as well as limits <m>t_{max}</m> and <m>x_{max}</m> of the graph.</p>

  </stack>
 -->
  <stack>
    <p><m>r = </m> <mathInput name="r" prefill="$rDefault" /></p>
    <p><m>\alpha = </m> <mathInput name="alpha" prefill="$alphaDefault" /></p>
    <p><m>\beta =</m> <mathInput name="beta" prefill="$betaDefault" /></p>
    <p><m>t_{max} = </m> <mathInput name="tmax" prefill="$tmaxDefault" /></p>
    <p><m>x_{max}=</m> <mathInput name="xmax" prefill="$xmaxDefault" /></p>
  </stack>

  <stack>
    <triggerSet>
      <updateValue target="$r" newValue="$rDefault" />
      <updateValue target="$alpha" newValue="$alphaDefault" />
      <updateValue target="$beta" newValue="$betaDefault" />
      <updateValue target="$tmax" newValue="$tmaxDefault" />
      <updateValue target="$xmax" newValue="$xmaxDefault" />
      <label>Reset parameters</label>
    </triggerSet>
  </stack>

</sideBySide>

</aside>


<number fixed="true" hide="true" name="zeroFixed">0</number>
<number hide="true" name="nan">0/0</number>
<conditionalContent hide="true" name="ft_NaN_to_infinity">
  <case condition="$$f($t)=$nan">
    <math>infinity</math>
  </case>
  <else>
    $$f($t)
  </else>
</conditionalContent>
  
<animateFromSequence name="timeAnimation" target="$t.value" from="0" to="$tmax" step="0.1" animationInterval="100" animationMode="increase once" animationOn="false" />


<p>You can explore the behavior of this model in the context of an anteater population <ref to="doenet:7BRujyNVd5uNj6H645HZFg">here</ref>.</p>
